  "vendor_website": "novus.com.br",
  "description": "Temperature controller with optional RS485 Modbus RTU: setpoint, process value, output power, status, PID and alarm settings, input and communication settings",
  "revision": 1,
  "firmware": "Communication protocol for software V2.2x",
  "source": "Novus N1040 temperature controller, communication protocol V2.2x A (Portuguese)",
  "sources": [
    {
      "title": "Controlador N1040 - Controlador de Temperatura - Protocolo de Comunicação",
      "version": "V2.2x A",
      "url": "https://www.novus.com.br/pt/produto/controladores/downloads2/getFile.asp?ID=321c65df18&Extensao=PDF",
      "accessed": "2026-11-14",
      "sha256": "b7b73fabb7e0bc4222166744455d06c0744488251632c9198a92dfb8e63ffb2e",
      "note": "linked in issue #437; register table, status words, coil table and I/O functions"
    }
  ],
  "notes": [
    "Modbus RTU needs the optional RS485 interface. Functions 03, 05 and 06; writes with address 0 are broadcast and reads in broadcast get no answer.",
    "1200 to 115200 baud, 8 data bits; even or odd parity with 1 stop bit, or no parity with 2 stop bits.",
    "Every register is a signed 16-bit value (two's complement). Temperatures, setpoints, limits and offsets are integers in the display unit, with the decimal places set in register 73 (dppo).",
    "A write outside the allowed range is not refused: the controller stores the nearest limit and returns it.",
    "The outputs can be written as coils only when the I/O function is Off.",
    "Written from the manufacturer's manual; not tested on a device."
  ],
  "protocol": "rtu",
  "databits": 8,
  "byte_order": "big",
  "address_base": 0,
  "x_status": "official",
